      "cadence": "weekly",
      "description": "60-90 min on the current rung's chosen challenge (see the rung\nbrief task \u2014 if this is the rung's first session, spend the first\n15 min picking one of its 3 options and noting why in the ADR).\nADR before code. The problems you hit here are what pull reading\nand feed Anki.\n\nGetting-into-the-groove rule: the first 10 min are always the same \u2014\nre-read the brief, write down the next smallest step, do that step.\nNo blank-page staring.\n\nAI assist rule: Claude may list options or point at docs. Stuck >30 min \u2192 ask for a hint, never the solution. Claude does not write the code in this slot.\n\nClose every session by asking Claude: 'What did I just build that has a known failure mode?' Add the answer to the reflection's dive-deeper list.\n\nCrunch week? This session + Anki + Saturday review is the whole week.\n",
